WEBVTT

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.210
ashita he tsuzuku sakamichi no tochuu de

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.210
On the uphill road that leads to tomorrow

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.510
surechigau otona tachi wa tsubuyaku no sa

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.510
We pass by adults who tell us this

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.640
"ai toka yume toka risou mo wakaru kedo

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.640
"I can understand ideals such as love and dreams

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.810
me no mae no genjitsu wa sonna ni amaku nai" tte

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.810
but the real world isn't as easy as you think"

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.150
tsumazuki nagara mo korogari nagara mo

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.150
Even though we keep tripping and falling

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.360
kasabuta darake no jyounetsu wo wasuretaku nai

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.360
We have to remember these pains of growing up

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.830
otona ni narenai bokura no

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.830
For all of us who can't force ourselves to do so yet

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.330
tsuyogari wo hitotsu kiite kure

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.330
Listen to this one thing I have to say

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.540
nige mo kakure mo shinai kara

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.540
I won't run or cower away

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.460
waraitai yatsu dake warae

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.460
So whoever wants to laugh at me, go ahead

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.250
semete tayori nai bokura no

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.250
Since we can't be relied upon yet

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.800
jiyuu no me wo tsumitoranai de

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.800
Don't take away our seed of freedom

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.800
mizu wo ageru sono yakume wo

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.800
The task of nurturing this plant

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.890
hataseba iindarou?

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.890
That's all we have to do, right?

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:30.020
{Intro}

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:32.780
Juron!

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.710
We can use this up to six times in a row!

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.540
Just using that will be great.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.420
Next, let's try a moving target.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:56.930
{Part A}

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:05.390
Botanical Garden Duel

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.780
Today's the day I make friends!

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:20.990
Okay!

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:39.930
Stop it!

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.340
That tickles!

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.140
Do you want to be my friend?

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.940
Oh, sorry!

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.900
Oh, Naomi-chan!

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.860
I thought you would always be alone,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.490
but it looks like you've
finally made a friend, huh?

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.280
Yeah! He's my friend!

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.490
What's his name?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:05.200
Oh yeah, what is your name?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.830
Schneider!

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.830
"Meru" doesn't mean anything in particular.
It's just something Schneider says.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.790
Noisy dog, isn't he?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.050
That's a weird bark...

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.220
I dare you to try saying "Wan!"

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.220
"Wan" is the Japanese equivalent of "woof."

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.150
My friend!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.030
Looks like you're all alone again.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.620
By the way, Gash...

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:44.530
Huh?

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.750
This Sunday, I get to go to the zoo.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.710
I bet you're jealous!

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:54.830
I wonder where lonely Gash gets to go.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.600
What a big tree!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.310
Huge leaves!

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.980
Mochinoki Municipal
Botanical Garden

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.440
Botanical Garden!

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.740
Kiyomaro! Kiyomaro!

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.620
Takamine-kun! Takamine-kun!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.700
You guys are goofing off way too much!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.160
There are a lot of delicate plants here!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.790
Be careful that you don't
tear things like leaves off!

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.590
Why do I have to be the one
to take care of these guys?

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:43.550
Kiyomaro! Take me somewhere!

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:44.590
Are we going?

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:45.840
Are we going?!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.890
Stop looking anywhere but here!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.010
Pretty please!

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.690
And somehow, even Mizuno
ended up coming along.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.060
This is fun!

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.150
I'm so happy!

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.110
Well, I guess it's okay sometimes.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.950
But, it's still as empty as ever here, eh?

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.750
Even though it's Sunday,
I can count all the visitors.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.920
What are you talking about?

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:23.260
Long time no see! I wonder why...

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.220
I'm a middle school student now.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.720
I'm busy with school every day.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.260
Oh, you're getting bullied then?

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:36.390
Shut up! I never said
anything about being bullied!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.320
Man, she's hard to talk to!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.320
Whee!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:49.160
You shouldn't let me catch you
off-guard like that, Kiyomaro!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.160
Hey!

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.660
You shouldn't play in
the botanical garden.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.830
It would be bad if something got injured.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.330
Oh, but you have no sympathy for me?

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.130
Who are you?

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.550
I am Kinoyama Tsukushi.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.590
I'm a caretaker here and
a friend to the plants.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.680
I am Gash Bell!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.680
I'm the one who fixed
Kiyomaro's temperament!

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:16.980
Really?

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:21.940
Really! Thanks to me, Kiyomaro has
made countless friends!

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:22.940
That's right!

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.360
There's Suzume and...

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.160
Don't laugh so much!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.330
But, you go to school now, don't you?

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.740
Whatever!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.200
Wait!

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.460
Are you one of Kiyomaro's
friends, Tsukushi?

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.580
I wouldn't go so far as to say "friend," but...

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:44.590
when he skipped class,
he came here a lot.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.920
He'd always read books alone.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:49.550
I just watched.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:53.890
I think he just needed a place to run
to when things were difficult.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.520
So you protected Kiyomaro?

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.810
It's not like that. I
didn't really do anything.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.860
You're a good person!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.480
Can I be your friend, too?

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.990
Sure! I'd be happy to.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.910
Takamine-kun! Takamine-kun!
I'm going to the orchard!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.910
Hey! Don't pick any fruit!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.290
Okay!

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.290
Ah, it's finally quiet.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.000
Huh? This is...

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.630
What is this? What can make
these sort of marks on a tree?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.720
This was not made by nature.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.050
Something really strong strangled it...

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:36.720
It couldn't be...!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:39.230
Opponents will come to fight you.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:40.890
It couldn't be...!

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:41.890
Juron!

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:49.990
What?!

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:50.990
This is...!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.820
Gash! It's a demon!
A guy with a book is nearby!

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.950
What?! Then he's aiming for us?!

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:01.910
No. If he came for us,
he would've confronted us directly.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.420
But he's attacking indiscriminately.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.590
Kiyomaro! What are you...

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.510
Tsukushi!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:14.720
What's this? I haven't
caught everyone yet?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.390
We're just training.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.350
"Training," you say?!

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.480
I haven't caught you yet.
 Why are you still here?

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:27.570
That's right. We're training.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.240
Without some sort of practice,
one can't get good, right?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:35.320
I'll give you thirty seconds
to run for your life.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.030
After that, you'll end up like this!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:40.750
Zakeru!

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.250
What?!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:46.960
Impossible!

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.550
This guy too?!

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:56.300
- This way, Gash!
- Kiyomaro, where are we going?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.810
The bad guy's over there!
Why are we running the other way?!

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.520
Are you running away?!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.600
Kiyomaro?!

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.440
Kiyomaro?

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.070
Ahh! I want to pick one!

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.900
But Takamine-kun would get angry.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.570
Ahh! But I want to pick one!

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:18.620
Tsukushi, I'm sorry.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:20.950
Your friends might get a little hurt...

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.160
but I'll get that bastard,
no matter what it takes.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.830
Kiyomaro...

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.000
Gash, I want you to listen carefully.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.460
We're at a disadvantage
against the enemy.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:35.680
Fighting a guy that can control plants
in a botanical garden is too reckless.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:41.180
That's why... we absolutely
must not lose to him!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.190
Gash, I want you to listen carefully
to my instructions from now on.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.360
In this fight, I'm going to
ask you to do two things.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.320
Damn. So this guy is just like me.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.440
He carries a book and uses a demon.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.660
That's precisely why it's good.
 It'll be good training.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:02.830
Exactly. This place has
so many plants to destroy.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.540
I can bring you to use 120% of your power.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:10.790
And as for that guy, he's a
lightning-shooting type.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:16.010
I've fought his type before, so
I already know his weakness.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.430
This match is ours!

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:28.020
{Part B}

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.860
Next, we find out where that guy is.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:46.700
I don't know his exact location, but he's still in this park.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.540
He's still in the park, so he hasn't left.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.710
This guy still wants to fight, eh?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.500
All right then, come out.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:55.710
Come out!

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:57.880
He's here!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.510
Behind us! There's the next one!

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:00.510
Ready!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.470
What?!

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.760
Zakeru!

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:08.140
He's fast! We should attack from behind!

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:11.810
Ready!

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.270
Zakeru!

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:19.650
Why? Their combination attack should
be weak against pincer attacks.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:26.200
The lightning-shooting types always hesitate unless
they're breathing together with the book user.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.290
Even so, this guy...

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.500
Bastard!

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.710
In that case, we'll just attack
from all sides and directions!

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:38.050
What? He ran away?

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.050
Follow him!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.300
All right! It's going great,

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.050
just like Kiyomaro said it would.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.180
Gash, I want you to listen carefully
to my instructions from now on.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.850
In this fight, I'm going to
ask you to do two things.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.400
The first thing is "formation."

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.360
This fight will demand more speed.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:04.570
Because of that, every time I tell you to face
a direction, it means we're being attacked.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:09.910
Starting now, you should follow
one meter behind me.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:13.000
Finally, always watch my right hand.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.960
When we attack, I'll point my fingers.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.210
Then you immediately
aim in that direction.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.760
Zakeru!

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.680
Don't underestimate me!

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.760
Juron!

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.270
Zakeru!

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:37.270
With this system, Zakeru's speed
works to our advantage.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.320
We'll also be able to attack
the enemy swiftly.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.570
With that...

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.240
our chances of nailing that guy
are remarkably better!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:53.620
You bastards, how long
do you plan on running?!

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.670
If you're going to fight, stop using
your legs and look over here!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.630
Attacking while you're running...

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.340
you haven't hit me once!

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:02.210
Bastards...

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.590
Still running away?!

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.220
Wait, Haruhiko!

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.890
Haven't you realized it?

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:07.930
What?

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.100
Number and strength.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:13.430
You're right.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.230
Those guys are still...

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.270
And one more thing.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.490
The second thing
I want to ask you for is...

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.410
I finally found you!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.120
So, not running away this time?

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:35.580
Finally decided to fight?!

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.630
Where did your human friend go?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.380
What's he doing?

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:44.800
Trying to run away alone?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.720
That's...!

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:50.510
That's the old guy I used for training!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.930
It can't be...!

00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:58.900
They're all gone!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.860
How?! Where did that power come from?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.860
Attacking while you're running...

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:07.570
you haven't hit me once!

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:08.570
It can't be...

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:12.240
The lightning that didn't hit me
wasn't even aimed at me?

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.330
It was actually aimed behind me
to rescue the hostages?

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.330
Hang in there, mister.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.790
We're almost to the exit!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.580
Damn you!

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:23.340
Saving them and making fun of me?!

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.510
Juron!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:27.840
What?!

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.470
Sorry, but I have to stop you here!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.430
Move, brat!

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.680
You guys did things you shouldn't have!

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:40.270
It's supposed to be a stupid fight to decide
the next king of the demon world!

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.980
But you dragged bystanders
in and hurt them!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.190
What's wrong with that?!

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.200
It's Kiyomaro's wish...

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:52.280
to rescue everyone who got
mixed into the fight!

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:53.780
So, he said...

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:57.120
And the second thing
I want to ask you for...

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:02.670
That's why Kiyomaro said we
need the desire to protect.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:06.880
Where am I?

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.920
Thank goodness. You came to!

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.390
It's okay now. You were rescued!

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.470
This is everyone, right?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.390
Ah! I want to pick one!

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:19.850
What should I do?

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.900
Everyone, please get out of here quickly!

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.570
Kiyomaro! Where are you going?

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:27.940
Gash...

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:30.280
is waiting for me!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.240
Still resisting?

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.910
Just give up, and get out of my way!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:42.880
Not yet!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.500
Stubborn little brat...

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:48.590
Like Kiyomaro said,
the desire to protect...

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.090
the desire to protect gives you strength!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:52.800
Desire to protect?

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.930
That's great! You're such
an idiot, it makes me laugh!

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:00.560
Kiyomaro will be back soon!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:04.980
It doesn't matter if you guys
are laughing like that now...

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.230
I wonder if we will...

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:08.690
What?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.450
Gash! Sorry I kept you waiting.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.070
Kiyomaro, how's everyone?

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:14.070
Everyone's safe.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.080
The only thing left is to beat
the crap out of this guy!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:21.160
Beat the crap out of us?
Go ahead and try it. I'll let you.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.370
Zakeru!

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:27.210
Huh? The Zakeru didn't come out?

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.470
You really are totally clueless, aren't you?

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:39.600
Kiyomaro!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.520
Why? Why won't Zakeru appear?

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.020
I'll explain it to you, amateur.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:49.150
Your power to invoke spells isn't infinite.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.990
The energy to use them
comes from your body.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.950
That is to say, for example, your heart...

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.910
How many times have you cast that spell?

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.370
Ten times? I'm still at five times.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.620
I've been resting and
only using half my power,

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:05.290
while you've been off frolicking.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:06.790
I can still use my power.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:09.250
This match is over. Drop the book!

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.130
Let go of Kiyomaro!

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:13.720
Stupid brat!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:14.760
Juron!

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:19.890
I told you, I can still use my power.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.560
Gash! Gash!

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.440
The brat's finished.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.060
So, you're left, eh?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:32.190
Damn it! Damn it!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:35.070
Are your bones breaking? 
Or are you going to faint?

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.950
Which one's going to happen first?

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:39.030
We'll turn up the heat gradually.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.710
So, this is where you're drawing
that mysterious power from!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:45.910
Tsukushi!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.710
Tsukushi! Behind you!

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.050
Tsukushi!

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.340
Sorry. I failed.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:58.260
I'll try again!

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.680
What are you saying?!

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:00.800
You need to run away!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.060
Never! I can't forgive this guy!

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.980
He injured my friends!

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:07.440
He's not an opponent you
can do anything against!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.100
You want to become powerful?!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.690
I always thought so.

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:17.570
Your back always looked so lonely.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:23.240
I thought that if there was something
I could do, I'd do it.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.250
You and Gash-chan brought me outside
and told me to run, but I can't!

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.250
Because you're my precious friend!

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.250
You've already given me a lot of trouble.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.090
But it's good training, eh?

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:41.930
I'll finish you off with
my strongest attack!

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:49.980
I'm going to fight! Even though I'm alone!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.060
You're not alone!

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:54.650
I'm here.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:55.820
Moreover...

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:58.780
Gash-chan is here!

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.120
Kiyomaro!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.040
It's the desire to protect!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:13.290
A powerful feeling is rising in my heart.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.670
There's something I want to protect!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.760
I'm not alone!

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.470
Great, everyone's here!

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.560
Raajia Jugaro!

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.810
All right!
Let's go, Gash!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.770
Yeah!

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.480
We'll win this fight!

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:31.940
The second spell,

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:33.480
Rashirudo!

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.360
How?!

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.910
How do they still have po--

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.670
Now, do you have an idea of how

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.210
the people you hurt felt?

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.980
My legs don't want to stand up.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.440
Tsukushi, are you okay?

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.320
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:21.070
Tsukushi, I'm sorry.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:25.490
The plants you treasured...

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:29.500
We couldn't protect Tsukushi's friends.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.790
Now it's my turn to show you my ability!

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:37.800
If you look after injured plants,
they'll sprout new buds.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:41.010
It's because all of my friends are strong.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.550
The plants,

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:43.550
Kiyomaro,

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:45.840
and Gash-chan, too!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.520
Everybody!

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.440
I'm back!

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.230
I-I completely forgot!

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:58.820
Suzume is completely unharmed?!

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.150
Takamine-kun!

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.700
Gash-kun!

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:05.030
{Ending}

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:20.750
ne konna koto tsuzukete itemo

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:20.750
You know, even if we continue to progress like this

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.970
shiawase wa mitsukaru no kana?

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.970
Will we be able to find true happiness?

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:31.100
tarinai mono kazoete mitemo

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:31.100
When I try counting what is missing in my life

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:36.230
kiri ga nai no wakatteru you

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:36.230
I know the list will keep going on and on

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:41.900
shinario douri nante

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:41.900
Everything goes according to plans

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:46.660
umaku iku wake nai kara

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:46.660
Of course that can never happen

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.280
toki ni wa zenbu

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.280
At times, everything that I have

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:52.120
nagedashi taku naru

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:52.120
I just want to let it all go

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:57.920
sonna hi ga attemo iiyone

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:57.920
Is it uncommon to have days like this?

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:05.470
hito wa mina okubyou dakara

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:05.470
Everyone is afraid, even though we don't show it

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:10.010
yume wo miru no kana?

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:10.010
Is that why we dream?

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:15.850
hito wa mina kodoku dakara

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:15.850
Everyone feels lonely on the inside

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:20.360
ai wo sagasu no kana?

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:20.360
Is that why we look for love?

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:23.400
kitto chigau

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:23.400
Even though you are not here

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:25.780
basho de kimi mo

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:25.780
know that where ever you are

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.950
onaji tsuki wo

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.950
You are gazing up

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:31.620
miteru you ne...

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:31.620
at the same moon as me...

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:35.080
{Preview}

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:41.210
I know that book user.

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:44.960
She makes dolls for her little sister
and carries her home from the park.

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:46.920
She's such a nice older sister!

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:48.050
Gash?

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:51.300
I can't fight them!

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:52.970
What are you talking about?!

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:54.140
They're attacking us!

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:56.270
Next time on Konjiki no Gash Bell:

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:58.480
The Kind Demon Koruru.

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:02.110
Why are those girls
crying while they fight?!

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:04.980
The Kind Demon Koruru
